<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1996/31/eng@/~part_IV__cl_26__subsec_5> <https://schema.org/text> "Where a notice of opposition is given in accordance with subsection (3), the Registrar shall, after giving the opponent and the applicant for restoration an opportunity to be heard, decide the matter, and where he decides to restore the registration, the registration shall have effect as if it had not lapsed, and he shall publish a notice in the Gazette that the registration has been so restored."@en <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1996/31/eng@> .
<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1996/31/eng@/~part_IV__cl_26__subsec_6> <http://data.europa.eu/eli/ontology#is_part_of> <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1996/31/eng@/~part_IV__cl_26> <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1996/31/eng@> .
